---
/**
 * @file SilenceMoment.astro
 * @description One quiet beat between Vox memoriae (II) and the catalog of past concerts.
 *  The word is the moment: in a part-book, tacet instructs the voice to stay silent — here
 *  the page rests before the voice enters (VoxMoment follows). No attribution, no aphorism.
 *
 *  The pacing is spatial, NOT behavioural: the section's own height supplies the pause. The
 *  page never touches the visitor's scroll — an earlier version halted Lenis for ~2.8s and read
 *  as a frozen page on touch, so the lock was removed for good (see the note where
 *  setupSilenceMoment used to live in scripts/landing.ts).
 *
 *  The arrival is a `.reveal-cue`, like the interludes and the coda: the shared observer flips
 *  `.is-in` when the visitor actually reaches the section, and 10-silence.css draws the
 *  ornament outward from its centre dot before `tacet.` is inked behind it. This replaced a
 *  controller that resolved both states at bind time — the entrance played out while the
 *  visitor was still in the hero, so the moment was always already over on arrival.
 *  Reduced-motion + no-JS visitors see the line statically (gated by html.voct-motion).
 * @architecture Astro islands 2026
 * @module components/landing/SilenceMoment
 */
---

<section class="silence-moment" aria-label="Chwila ciszy">
  <div class="silence-inner reveal-cue">
    <svg
      class="silence-ornament"
      viewBox="0 0 120 12"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      {/* Both rules start AT the dot and are drawn outward, so the ornament opens from its
          centre rather than sweeping across. Stroke-dash drawing always runs from x1, so the
          left rule is authored right-to-left (50 → 0) — reversing the coordinates is the only
          way to reverse the direction. pathLength="1" puts both on the same clock. */}
      <line class="silence-rule" pathLength="1" x1="50" y1="6" x2="0" y2="6" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-opacity="0.45" />
      <circle class="silence-dot" cx="60" cy="6" r="1.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
      <line class="silence-rule" pathLength="1" x1="70" y1="6" x2="120" y2="6" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-opacity="0.45" />
    </svg>

    <p class="silence-line">
      <em>tacet.</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
